  "details": "The paid nameplate theme \"Electric Pulse\" (the heart-themed one) is not being displayed correctly to other users.\n\nIssue:\n\nWhen I equip the Electric Pulse nameplate theme, it appears correctly from my own view. However, other users report that my nameplate looks like the default/standard nameplate — the theme is not applied at all from their perspective. This happens for everyone who sees me, not just specific users.\n\nWhat I've tried:\n\nSwitching to other nameplate themes works fine — those themes are correctly visible to other users. The problem only occurs with Electric Pulse.\n\nExpected behavior:\n\nThe Electric Pulse theme should be visible to all other users, the same as other nameplate themes.\n\nActual behavior:\n\nElectric Pulse only renders for myself; everyone else sees the default nameplate.\n\nSince Electric Pulse is a paid theme, I'd really appreciate a fix. Thank you!",
